As far as I can makes out:
unless you're a role that can get two-weaponing to expert, the
difference between a sabre or a katana in the off-hand is only 1 point
in terms of weapon damage (assuming two-weapon is at skilled), and
your off-hand weapon is never used in calculating to-hit bonus.
Therefore I suspect that the sabre will be more effective in an area
where silver-hating monsters are common.

In fact, even if long sword and and two-weaponing are both at expert,
it seems the difference in damage between it and the saber is still
only two points, or 2-6, if you take account of the katana's d12 vs
saber's d8 (vs non-silver-hating large monsters). Against small
monsters it's only 2-4 (katana d10).  I'm sure the +d20 means the
silver saber wins hands down even if less than half the monsters you
meet take silver damage.

Now, if it's a choice between a +7 katana and a +0 silver saber,
that's another matter, of course!  Or you could keep changing your
weapon depending on what you're fighting - that would be the smart but
tedious tactic, I suppose...

Just worth considering, depending on how many silver hating monsters
there are where you are.

